WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.967
Stable Diffusion.

2
00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:06.667
One architectural move makes diffusion cheap enough for consumer hardware.

3
00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:10.233
Stable Diffusion is latent diffusion.

4
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:13.653
Denoising in pixel space is brutally expensive.

5
00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:18.167
One small image has about seven hundred eighty six thousand numbers.

6
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.967
So instead, we denoise a compressed latent.

7
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.367
Here's the pipeline.

8
00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:26.200
The prompt is encoded by a CLIP text encoder.

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.966
A pretrained VAE has compressed images into a sixty four by sixty four by four latent,

10
00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:34.000
about forty eight times smaller.

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.961
The U-Net does all its denoising steps in that small space,

12
00:00:37.961 --> 00:00:40.567
with the prompt attended to at every step.

13
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:45.133
Finally the VAE decoder inflates the clean latent back to pixels.

14
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:49.100
Text steers generation through cross-attention.

15
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.233
The prompt becomes text embeddings.

16
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:54.333
The U-Net's attention layers attend over them.

17
00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:57.043
And this happens at every denoising step.

18
00:00:57.043 --> 00:01:00.333
The prompt whispers into every step, not just the start.

19
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:03.633
The practical knob is guidance scale.

20
00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:06.526
Each step extrapolates toward the prompt.

21
00:01:06.526 --> 00:01:08.867
Low values are imaginative but loose.

22
00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.700
Around seven point five is the sweet spot.

23
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.940
High values, twelve to fifteen, follow the prompt literally,

24
00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.567
but with fried, oversaturated artifacts.

25
00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.167
Here's the sweep in code.

26
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:25.200
We load the pipeline in half precision on a consumer GPU.

27
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.300
Then we generate the same prompt with the same seed at five guidance values, and save each image.

28
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.867
A good way to keep this.

29
00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:38.067
You generate concept art with the sweep and keep the five image strip.

30
00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:43.467
When an interviewer asks how Stable Diffusion runs on a laptop, you answer in one breath.

31
00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.547
It doesn't diffuse pixels.

32
00:01:45.547 --> 00:01:49.312
A VAE compresses to a latent, the U-Net denoises there,

33
00:01:49.312 --> 00:01:52.667
and guidance is the literal versus creative dial.

34
00:01:53.867 --> 00:01:54.644
Let's recap.

35
00:01:54.644 --> 00:01:57.233
Denoise a compressed latent, not pixels.

36
00:01:57.533 --> 00:02:00.433
A VAE encodes and decodes that small space.

37
00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:03.733
The prompt enters through cross-attention at every step.

38
00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:07.567
And guidance scale trades creativity for literalness.

39
00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:08.500
Next up: GANs.
